P71,2,5f4aa7d425629f5291aca6fc,Lambda functions can be a useful tool in programming for a number of reasons. They allow for concise function definitions in a single line of code which can make code easier to read and write. When used as arguments in function calls lambda functions can reduce the number of lines needed to express an operation and make code more readable. Lambda functions are also flexible and can be defined on the fly making them useful for operations that are only used once and don't need to be named or saved for later use. For those familiar with functional programming concepts lambda functions can be more intuitive to use than traditional function definitions.,Readability/Understandability
